NAME="Nyx Linux"
PRETTY_NAME="Nyx Linux"
ID=arch
ID_LIKE=arch
VERSION="@RELEASE@"
VERSION_ID="@RELEASE@"
PRETTY_VERSION="Nyx Linux @RELEASE@"
BUILD_ID="nyx"
ANSI_COLOR="0;36"
# The name says Nyx Linux and nothing else. "Arch-based" used to sit in
# PRETTY_NAME, VARIANT and PRETTY_VERSION, and it came from nowhere useful: the
# user interface shows PRETTY_NAME, so the installer announced itself as "Nyx
# Linux (Arch-based) has been installed" and the window title carried the same
# parentheses.
#
# What it did not do was make the base any less Arch. ID=arch and ID_LIKE=arch
# are what pacman reads to decide compatibility, what makes Arch packages
# installable, and what a reader of this file can verify. They stay exactly as
# they were, because a claim that can be checked is worth more than a claim in
# brackets. The base is stated plainly in README.md, README.ru.md and NOTICE,
# where attribution belongs.
#
# VARIANT is gone rather than emptied: it only ever held "Arch-based", and an
# empty VARIANT is worse than no key at all.
# Add GitHub project, support, and release URLs here when the repository is published.
